From: j7
Subject: j7: leave the CPU clock off until the mux map is confirmed

The two boots that asked for 1794 MHz both stopped before the logo and left no new log: 0395
parked the cores on the MIF switch, 0396 on the oscillator, and neither came back.  The raise runs
in AppleCLCD::start, before the kernel ever flushes its ring to storage, so a core that stops there
writes nothing anywhere and leaves the previous boot's log in place - which is exactly what the
phone showed both times.

That is not a reason to keep spending flashes on it: 0380 already measured what a wrong ARMCLK
move costs (cpu_mhz=38), and the evidence now points at the mux map itself rather than at the
switch or the oscillator.  j7cpu now defaults to 0, so the image boots at the bootloader's 902 MHz
operating point - the state every log so far was recorded in - and j7_cpu_clock() still exists for
an explicit j7cpu=1794 test once the vendor ARMCLK mux register is confirmed.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -675,10 +675,17 @@
 		}
 	}
 	{
-		/* j7cpu=<kHz> raises both clusters to that top DVFS step; the vendor table's
-		 * cl0_max_support_idx row is 1794 MHz, and 0 keeps the bootloader's 902 MHz.
-		 * A small value is MHz. */
-		int cpu = 1794;
+		/* j7cpu=<kHz> raises both clusters to that top DVFS step; 0 - the default -
+		 * leaves the bootloader's 902 MHz operating point alone.  A small value is MHz.
+		 *
+		 * It is off by default because both boots that asked for the top step stopped
+		 * before the logo and left no new log: 0395 parked the cores on the MIF switch,
+		 * 0396 on the oscillator, and neither came back.  Whatever stops them lives in
+		 * the ARMCLK mux path this tree believes is +0x208 bit 12, and until that map is
+		 * confirmed against the vendor source a boot that asks for the top step costs
+		 * the phone its display and its log.  Pass j7cpu=1794 to try it with every other
+		 * part of the boot known good. */
+		int cpu = 0;
 		PE_parse_boot_argn("j7cpu", &cpu, sizeof(cpu));
 		if (cpu > 0 && cpu < 100000) {
 			cpu *= 1000;
